643, "Complete Basic Flight Training"

644, "Good morning pilot.  Don't touch the controls until told to do so."

645, "The first function you will learn is targeting. [Press $t$] Target me."

646, "In the lower left hand corner of your HUD is your Target View.  The top line displays the targeted ship's name and class."

647, "The next line shows the distance to your target and its speed."

648, "Note the brackets around my ship indicating I am your current target."

649, "As I fly out of view, the offscreen indicator will display.  It points in the direction you must turn in order to face your target."

650, "The circular gauge near the bottom of your HUD is the radar.  Friendly ships are shown in green.  Hostile ships appear as red."

651, "Using your main flight controller turn your ship toward mine.  Stop when my ship is in your center reticle."

652, "Good.  Now stay in that position."

653, "Now turn toward my ship again."

654, "[Press $m$] Match my speed."

655, "Match my speed now."

656, "To the left of the reticle is the speed gauge.  The capital M next to the current speed indicates that you are matching speed with your target."

657, "Now I want you to use your acceleration key, [$a$] to move to within 75 units of me.  Do not collide with my ship."

658, "Good.  Now decelerate [$z$] to drop 200 units behind me."

659, "Good.  Now the afterburner.  [$tab$]  Engage your afterburner."

660, "That extra speed is useful for quick evasive maneuvers.  Maintain your max top speed. [$\$].  Try it now."

661, "Now come to a complete stop. [$backspace$]"

662, "Drone 01 has just warped in.  Target it. [Press $t$]."

663, "A group of cargo containers has just warped in.  Target C-01a. [Press $t$]"

664, "Good.  Now inspect these cargo containers."

665, "The sound you heard indicates the cargo container has been inspected.  Notice the cargo display in the target box at your lower left."

666, "Near the center of your HUD the hull integrity of your target is displayed.  Notice that it has dropped from 100%."

667, "Now Destroy C-01a."

668, "Good.  Now destroy C-02b and C-03a.  Remember to target them [$t$]."

669, "Let's see how quickly you can destroy these new cargo containers.  Target them [$t$] and destroy them with your ML-16."

670, "Good job.  Now it's time to leave.  [Press $alt-j$]"

671, "Note how it moves as I fly around.  It is always pointing at your target."

672, "Notice how the triangles separate.  The farther apart they are, the farther you'll have to turn to face your target."

673, "Finally, note the number by the indicator.  This is the distance to your target."

674, "Good.  Now follow me.  Note how your speed automatically changes to match mine."

675, "The gauge to the left of your speed gauge indicates remaining afterburner power.  Note that it is consumed rapidly."

676, "Good.  Now fly within 100 units of it, then come to a stop.  [$backspace$]  Be careful not to fly too fast."

677, "Well done.  Note that it takes some time to come to a complete stop."

678, "In order to determine the contents of a ship or cargo container, you must target it, face it, and fly within 150 units."

679, "Now, fire your primary weapon [press $left ctrl$] at C-01a.  Hit it a few times, but do not destroy it."

680, "This information is also available in the upper right of your target display."

681, "Good job."

682, "Inability to follow instructions results in immediate failure.  Jump back to base to reschedule training Phase 1.  [Press $alt-j$]"

683, "Training Mission 2"

684, "This is a basic training mission.  Part 2 of 3.
The player learns subsystem targeting, how to toggle primary weapons, and about the effects of the Disruptor."

685, "Welcome to Phase Two of your basic training."

686, "A cargo container will be delivered to the training area.  You will be expected to demonstrate the targeting and firing skills that you acquired in Phase One of your training."

687, "After reviewing Phase one of your training, you will learn advanced targeting and firing techniques."

688, "You were proficient in meeting the requirements for all of your training objectives.  As a result, you are qualified to advance to Phase Three of basic training.  Congratulations."

689, "You were unsuccessful in your attempts to meet the requirements for Phase Two of your training.  Advancement to Phase Three of basic training is dependent upon successful completion of all Phase Two exercises."

690, "Your objective is to destroy the ship's subsystems, not the ship.  Using only your disruptor cannon will allow you to destroy the subsystems without destroying the drone."

691, "Don't shoot at your instructor."

692, "Target the Cargo"

693, "Destroy the Cargo"

694, "Press $Left Ctrl$"

695, "Switch Primary Weapons"

696, "Press $.$"

697, "Target Drone A"

698, "Target Drill Instructor"

699, "Press $h$"

700, "Target Drone A Sensors"

701, "Press $s$"

702, "Destroy Drone A sensors"

703, "Target Drone B Sensors"

704, "Press $h$ Press $s$"

705, "Destroy Drone B"

706, "Press $spacebar$"

707, "Destroy Drone A Weapons"

708, "Jump Back to Base"

709, "Return to Base"

710, "Complete Basic Combat Training"

711, "Welcome to Phase Two of your training."

712, "First, target the cargo container.  Cycle through all objects in the area until the cargo is targeted.  [Press $t$]"

713, "Destroy the cargo container with your ML-16.  [Press $Left Ctrl$]"

714, "Nice shooting."

715, "Switch your primary weapon from the ML-16 to the disruptor.  [Press $.$]"

716, "Good."

717, "The Disruptor is an energy weapon that destroys the subsystems of a target, doing only minimal damage to the target's hull."

718, "Two practice drones will be used for this phase of the training."

719, "Target Drone A."

720, "Now target my ship, Pilot."

721, "All right."

722, "You have a targeting control which allows you to target the nearest hostile target [$h$].  If pressed again quickly, it will target the next nearest hostile object."

723, "Target Drone A using your hostile targeting control.  [Press $h$]"

724, "You can also target ship subsystems [$s$].  By pressing the subsystem targeting control repeatedly, you can cycle your through the subsystems of your target."

725, "When a subsystem is targeted, it is outlined by a large square.  If the targeted object is not in view, it will be marked by a diamond."

726, "Target the sensors on Drone A.  [Press $s$]"

727, "Nice work."

728, "You will use the Disruptor to destroy the subsystems of an enemy ship when you do not wish to destroy the ship.  Destroy the sensors on Drone A using the Disruptor.  [Press $Left Ctrl$]"

729, "Why did you do that?  Go back to base, review the basics, then come back to training when you are ready to learn."

730, "Target the sensors on Drone B."

731, "Notice the sensors on Drone B are not in your direct line of sight, even though you have it targeted.  The diamond indicates where the subsystem is located.  It is also indicated in the HUD target monitor."

732, "Follow me, Pilot."

733, "Now you should have line of sight to the Sensors of Drone B.  If not, move your ship until you are facing the Sensors subsystem."

734, "When ordered, you will fire your secondary weapon at Drone B. [$spacebar$]"

735, "The MX-50 is a heat-seeking missile.  When you are ordered to fire upon Drone B, the MX-50 will home in on your target."

736, "Destroy Drone B using the MX-50.  [Press $spacebar$]"

737, "Good shooting!"

738, "You have proven successful.  Good job."

739, "Fine job, Pilot."

740, "I'm not going to wait all day for you, Pilot."

741, "Large drones will be used for this phase of your training."

742, "That is all for today's training.  I'm going to destroy Drone A.  Feel free to join me, Pilot."

743, "Activate your jump drive and head back to base.  [Press $Alt-J$]"

744, "Now destroy the weapon subsystems on Drone A.  Do it without destroying the drone."

745, "Training Mission 3"

746, "Welcome to the final phase of basic training.  In this phase, your dogfight ability will be put to the test."

747, "You will be required to engage multiple waves of fighter drones.  Some will be armed.  You are expected to destroy as many of them as possible.  Good luck."

748, "You destroyed all ten drones.  Congratulations.  This completes your basic training.  Welcome to the GTA League of Defense."

749, "You were unable to destroy all of the drones.  Dogfighting skills are what keep pilots alive and will win this war.  Without them you cannot be accepted into the ranks of the GTA League of Defense."

750, "Practice your dogfighting skills."

751, "Don't shoot at your Instructor."

752, "Target Drone"

753, "Destroy Drone"

754, "Destroy 2 and 3"

755, "Destroy 5 and 6"

756, "Destroy Drone 4"

757, "Destroy Drone 7"

758, "Destroy 8 and 9"

759, "Destroy 10 and 11"

760, "Destroy 12 and 13"

761, "Destroy 14 and 15"

762, "Destroy 16 and 17"

763, "Complete Basic Dogfight Training"

764, "Welcome to Phase Three of your training.  This phase will cover dog fighting techniques."

765, "First, target my ship.  [Press $T$]"

766, "You'll notice as I move, a circular indicator moves in front of my ship.  That is the lead indicator.  It indicates where you need to fire your primary weapon to hit your target."

767, "Target the unarmed drone that has just arrived.  [Press $T$]"

768, "The target box in the lower left-hand corner of the HUD displays the distance to and hull integrity of your target."

769, "Your target's hull strength is also shown in the lower part of your reticle."

770, "As I shoot the drone, notice its hull integrity drop slowly."

771, "A good dog fighting tactic is matching speeds with your target.  I want you to match speeds with the drone.  [Press $M$]"

772, "You should be on the move at all times during a dogfight.  Now destroy the drone."

773, "Don't forget you also have missiles.  [Press $spacebar$]"

774, "Two new unarmed drones have arrived.  Destroy both of them.  Remember to match their speed.  [Press $M$]"

775, "This drone is armed.  It will start firing upon you in as little as 10 seconds.  Destroy it."

776, "Pilot, what are you doing, taking this much damage from a drone?!  Imagine what the Vasudans will do to you!"

777, "Try this again.  Here come two more unarmed drones.  Destroy them."

778, "Here is an armed drone.  You have 10 seconds before it opens fire.  Destroy it."

779, "Pilot, you are by no means ready to go to battle.  Jump back to base for rescheduling of training Phase 3.  [Press $alt-j$]"

780, "Now comes the fun part.  Five pairs of armed drones will jump in.  Destroy as many as you can."

781, "Looks like you've had enough.  Report back to base.  [Press $alt-j$]"

782, "Inability to follow instructions results in immediate failure.  Jump back to base for rescheduling of training Phase 3.  [Press $alt-j$]"

783, "Great job, pilot.  Basic training is complete.  Return to base.  [Press $alt-j$]"

784, "Basic training is complete.  Let's head back to base.  [Press $alt-j$]"

785, "An easy way to target new hostiles is by using auto targeting.  [Press $alt-h$]  This will automatically target your nearest hostile after your current target has either left the area or has been destroyed."

786, "Basic Training Stage 4"

787, "Welcome to Advanced Training.  In today's course you will learn the basics of messaging, countermeasures, and the support ship."

788, "Well done Pilot.  You have completed phase one of advanced training."

789, "Why did you leave before the training was completed?  You need to stay for the whole lesson in order to get credit for completing the course."

790, "Do not leave the mission until the instructor tells you."

791, "Target Freighter 01"

792, "Call reinforcements"

793, "Press [$c$], [4], [1]"

794, "Order Disarm"

795, "Press [$c$], [2], [1], [3]"

796, "Order Disable"

797, "Press [$c$], [2], [1], [2]"

798, "Order Destroy"

799, "Press [$c$], [2], [1], [1]"

800, "Order Departure"

801, "Press [$c$], [2], [1], [0]"

802, "Launch Countermeasures"

803, "Press $x$"

804, "Call Support"

805, "Press [$c$], [5]"

806, "Complete Advanced Training"

807, "All right Alpha 1.  Now you're going to learn about messaging and countermeasures."

808, "Here comes your first target.  Go ahead and target Freighter 01."

809, "Good.  Now, call in some reinforcements.  Press the communications [$c$] key to bring up the messaging window.  From there, press the [4] key followed by the [1] key and your reinforcements will arrive."

810, "Now I am going to show you how to disarm your target using your wingmen.  Press the communications [$c$] key to bring up your messaging box again."

811, "Now, select [2] to send your orders to a wing rather than just a ship, then the [1] key to choose Epsilon wing.  By choosing Epsilon wing, you are sending your orders to that wing only.  Finally press the [3] key to ''Disarm Target''."

812, "Observe that your wingmen have made every effort not to destroy your target.  They will only attempt to disarm, thus making sure your target will no longer be able to attack you with any of its weapons."

813, "The next step will be to disable your target.  By giving this order to your wingmen, they will take out the engines of your target, thus disabling it from moving."

814, "You will once again bring up the messaging window by pressing the communications [$c$] key.  Next, select [2] for ''wing'', and [1] for ''Epsilon''.  Finally, press the [2] key to disable your target."

815, "As you can see, your wingmen are now taking out the engines of Freighter 01.  It won't take them long to knock out the engines of this freighter, but keep in mind that other targets can require many more hits to disable it than this freighter does."

816, "Now it's time to put that freighter out of its misery.  Order your wingmen to destroy the freighter."

817, "Well done pilot!"

818, "Press the communications [$c$] button to bring up the messaging window, followed by the [2] key to select a wing, then the [1] key to select Epsilon wing.  Finally press the [1] key to have them destroy your target."

819, "Well, how does it feel to have ordered your first kill?  Hope you enjoyed it because I want you to do it again."

820, "I want you to order Epsilon wing to destroy Freighter 02.  Have you remembered your previous instruction?  If you need to, you can look on your directives for previous instructions of this same goal."

821, "Nicely done Alpha 1.  I think you've got this down."

822, "OK pilot, now that you've had your fun I want to to order Epsilon wing to depart."

823, "All right pilot, now it's time to learn about countermeasures.  A countermeasure presents a new target for the pursuing missile to go after, thus causing the missile to avoid your ship.  As you will soon see this does not always work."

824, "For this lesson we are bringing in one of our Leviathan class cruisers.  Their gunner will be getting practice hitting a moving target, you.  Don't worry, these are just dummy missiles designed to give you a feel for live fire."

825, "In a few seconds the Neptune will begin to launch missiles at you.  Once the missiles are incoming, you will press the countermeasures [$x$] key to release your countermeasures."

826, "You should also immediately increase your forward velocity to maximum, and fly away from the pusuing missile.  In fact, you should be using your afterburners a great deal of the time."

827, "Then when the missile is nearly upon you, launch the countermeasure.  Listen to the beeping sound of the missile lock to gauge the distance of the missile.  The quicker the beeps, the closer the missile."

828, "While you are launching your countermeasures, you will also try turning your ship about in sharp movements.  This will further help you to avoid being hit by the missile."

829, "That gives us just enough time to squeeze in one more lesson."

830, "It's time for you to reload your countermeasures.  To do this you will need to call in a support ship."

831, "In order for the support ship to dock, you must bring your ship to a complete stop.  The support ship will then automatically dock with you.  Check your  indicator in the lower portion of the HUD which shows the ETA for the support ship."

832, "The support ship's primary purpose is twofold.  First, it will reload your ship with any secondary weapons and countermeasures."

833, "Finally, the support ship is capable of making minor repairs to you ship.  It can fully repair any damaged or destroyed subsystem on your ship.  However, the support ship is not capable of repairing your main hull."

834, "All right pilot, now for a little more paractice with countermeasures.  The Neptune is going to fire at you again.  Take evasive actions."

835, "All right Pilot, I believe that will be enough for today.  The Neptune needs to continue its training elsewhere and you've had enough for one day.  You've done a good job, considering you're just a rookie.  Return to base."

836, "First, make sure that you still have Freighter 01 targeted."

837, "To do this, press the communications [$c$] key to bring up the messaging window.  Select [2] for wing, and [1] for Epsilon.  Finally, press [0] for Depart."

838, "Don't worry, the missiles being fired at you are not armed and will not harm you at all."

839, "You will use your afterburners to help maintain a high speed.  Additionally, you should try to keep the missile pointer at a 3 or 9 o'clock position."

840, "You will do this by pressing the communications [$c$] key to bring up your messaging window, followed by the [5] key for Rearm."

841, "Check your indicator in the lower central portion of the HUD which shows the ETA for the support ship."

842, "Keep in mind a support ship can only load as many weapons as it has on board.  It may not be enough to fully reload you."

843, "When you have succesfully evaded a missile, an indicator will come up in the upper portion of your targeting reticle.  This will alert you to the fact that you indeed evaded the missile."

844, "Inability to follow instructions results in immediate failure.  Jump back to base to reschedule training phase one."

845, "Advanced Training #2"

846, "Training Mission #5.  Aspect seekers, shield system."

847, "Welcome to Advanced Training."

848, "As you know, research has been completed on the new shielding technology.  Shields are being added to all fighters and bombers.  In this training mission, you will be instructed on the use of your shield system."

849, "In addition to the shield technology, the new Interceptor aspect seeking missiles is now available.  They are more powerful than the MX-50s, but require a lock before they may be fired.  You will learn how to properly use the Interceptor in this mission."

850, "The shield is an important addition to your ship, and the Interceptors are a formidable addition to your arsenal.  You must learn how to use them well."

851, "Congratulations.  You have completed your training."

852, "You departed before completing training.  You must complete this training mission before continuing."

853, "Target Freighter 1"

854, "Press $H$"

855, "Fire Interceptor"

856, "Target Weapons subsystem"

857, "Destroy Weapons"

858, "Destroy Freighter 1"

859, "Destroy Drones"

860, "Destroy DroneB fighters"

861, "Balance Shields"

862, "Press $q$"

863, "Maximize Front Quadrant"

864, "Press $Up Arrow$"

865, "Maximize Rear Quadrant"

866, "Press $Down Arrow$"

867, "Complete Advanced Technology Training"

868, "All right.  First we'll cover use of the aspect seeking Interceptor missiles.  Note that you are fully equipped with Interceptors."

869, "Unlike heat seeking missiles, such as the MX-50, you must acquire a lock on your target in order for an aspect seeker to home."

870, "However, the aspect seeker is well worth this effort, as its homing ability is much stronger."

871, "Once fired, the aspect seeker will track its target anywhere in space.  Once the heat seeker loses track of its target, it is not likely to reacquire lock."

872, "Freighter 1 is now entering.  Let's see how you do with those Interceptors."

873, "Target the freighter. [Press $H$]"

874, "Notice the red indicator moving towards your target.  That's the Aspect Diamond.  Once it has moved onto your target, you'll see the lock indicator.  This indicates your Interceptors are locked and ready to fire."

875, "Now, fire one Interceptor at the freighter."

876, "Note how fast the Interceptor moves.  They also deliver quite a payload."

877, "Note that the Interceptor is nearly useless if fired before lock has been attained.  This is a crucial difference between the Interceptor and the MX-50."

878, "Now, target the Weapons subsystem on the freighter. [Press $S$ until targeted.]"

879, "Good.  Now, wait until you have attained lock on the Weapons subsystem."

880, "Now, fire your Interceptors until the Weapons subsystem has been destroyed."

881, "Well done.  Note your Interceptors will be effective in destroying subsystems on large targets."

882, "Now, unload your Interceptors until you've destroyed Freighter 1."

883, "Excellent job.  Now it's time to destroy some moving targets."

884, "A round of Interceptors can be fired every 3 seconds.  Fire another round and note the countdown timer in your Weapons Gauge."

885, "Your ship is equipped with the new shielding technology.  It is able to absorb a large amount of incoming weapon energy."

886, "As the shield absorbs damage, it becomes weaker.  However, it automatically regenerates itself over time."

887, "Your shield integrity gauge is located at the lower right of your HUD.  It is flashing now."

888, "Your shield is divided into four quadrants, each able to withstand a certain amount of damage."

889, "When a quadrant of your shield suffers damage, the corresponding section of your Shield Integrity gauge will flash.  Observe."

890, "Note the front of your shield is flashing as if you've taken damage."

891, "Note how the gauge changes as your shield takes more damage.  When a shield quadrant has been destroyed, all damage will pass through to the underlying hull."

892, "Note that your shield automatically recharges over time.  I will accelerate this process to save time."

893, "Now observe as the front quadrant of your shield repairs itself to full strength."

894, "Now your shield has recharged back to full strength.  Next we'll cover shield management."

895, "There are a number of ways you can manage your shield.  The simplest is the Equalize Quadrants function."

896, "Well done.  Note that your front section has been largely recharged.  This came at the expense of shield energy from the three other quadrants."

897, "I have damaged your front shield quadrant again.  Now use your Equalize Quadrants function to repair your front quadrant.  [Press $q$]"

898, "I'm now going to reduce most of your shield strength.  Note that three of your four quadrants are now near zero strength."

899, "Now you'll learn how to maximize shield strength in a specific quadrant."

900, "First, you'll maximize the strength in your front quadrant.  [Press $Up Arrow$ several times.]"

901, "Well done.  Note that your front quadrant is at full strength, while the others were drained."

902, "Maximizing your front shield quadrant is especially useful when you're attacking a large ship against its turret fire."

903, "Now I want you to maximize your rear shield quadrant.  [Press $Down Arrow$ several times.]"

904, "If you're pursuing an important objective and are being attacked from the rear, maximizing your rear shield quadrant can be very useful."

905, "Well done, Pilot.  Aspect seeking missiles are an important part of your arsenal.  Use them well."

906, "And proper shield management can make all the difference in a crucial battle."

907, "This concludes your training.  Return to base."

908, "In order to gain aspect lock on a moving target, you must keep the target's lock box in a fixed location inside your HUD reticle."

909, "I will now call in fighter drones.  When the first drone enters, target it and acquire lock.  Try to keep the target indicator in the center of your HUD reticle."

910, "Once you have acquired lock, fire an Interceptor to destroy the drone.  Note, these drones will not be using countermeasures."

911, "Well done.  Now let's try something a little more difficult.  Wings of two drones will appear at once.  Destroy them all."

912, "All right.  Now we'll move on to your shield system."

913, "Note that you'll need to be in range of these drones before you can gain aspect lock.  Fly towards them."

914, "You're low on Interceptors.  You should rearm soon. [Press $Shift-R$]"

915, "Eve of Destruction Redux"

916, "First mission in demo campaign for FreeSpace.  Redux."

917, "Pilot Attend:  Welcome to the $f GTD $f Galatea.  Your first assignment as a part of the $f Galatea's crew is to stand the 3rd watch.  You will patrol the area surrounding the $f GTC $f Orff.  The $f GTC $f Orff suffered an engine breakdown in the Betelgeuse system, and is awaiting repairs."

918, "You will be on watch with one other ship, $f Alpha $f 2.  Since this is your first watch, $f Alpha $f 2 will be piloted by Lt. Harbison, a seasoned veteran and top-notch pilot."

919, "You will begin your watch by jumping to Betelgeuse near the $f GTC $f Orff."

920, "We have reports of Vasudan fighters in this system, so stay alert.  Engage and destroy any hostiles that threaten the $f Orff."

921, "At the end of your watch, you will be relieved by $f Delta wing.  Upon $f Delta's arrival, you are to return to base."

922, "Your primary objective will be to protect the $f Orff until the end of your watch.  We expect you to carry out your orders to the letter."

923, "You may confirm your ship hardware and weapons loadout for this mission.  If found satisfactory, commit to the mission.  $f GTD $f Galatea quarterdeck signing off."

924, "The GTC Orff was destroyed during your watch.  Dozens of lives were lost due to your poor performance.  This catastrophe will surely result in an increased Vasudan presence in this system.

There is no place for you in the GTA.  You are dismissed."

925, "If you kill the Vasudan fighters before they reach the Orff, they will not be able to harm it.  Concentrate on one fighter at a time.  When it's destroyed, move to the next.  After Delta wing arrives, you may return to base."

926, "You did a fine job on your first watch, Pilot.  Your strong sense of duty will serve the Alliance well.

The presence of Vasudans in this system gives us little reason to worry.  The ships that attacked you and the Orff were probably remnants of the Vasudan convoy that we hit last week."

927, "Your performance was excellent.  We have no recommendations for you."

928, "Despite your efforts, Vasudan fighters escaped from the system.

If we allow them to elude us, pilot, we appear weak.  We won't tolerate this sort of embarrassment again."

929, "If you are having trouble killing the Vasudans, try launching missiles.  MX-50s automatically seek out a hostile target if it is within range.  After Delta arrives, you can still help them out by destroying more Vasudans."

930, "We are saddened to learn of Lieutenant Harbison's demise.  He was a brave and skillful pilot.  A memorial service will be held at 0930.  You are ordered to attend."

931, "Next time, try to ensure the safety of your wingmen.  If he requests help, engage the ship that's attacking him."

932, "You left the field of battle before your watch was ended.  This act of cowardice will stain your record for the rest of your military career.

You are suspended from flight duty.  Dismissed."

933, "Never leave a battle until you are sure the battle is over.  Wait until all Primary mission goals are resolved, or you are ordered to return to base."

934, "Repair crew"

935, "Destroy Virgo"

936, "Destroy Cancer"

937, "Destroy Aries"

938, "Destroy Pisces"

939, "Protect the GTC Orff"

940, "Assist Delta with their Watch"

941, "Hey there, Alpha 1.  I hear you're new to the Galatea."

942, "Just follow my lead... you'll be fine."

943, "Turn on your Autotargeting."

944, "We've got company!  Break and attack!"

945, "The first one's hull is down to 40%.  Looks like they've already seen some action.  Let's finish them off."

946, "Make sure they don't reach the Orff, pilot!"

947, "This looks like more than a scouting wave."

948, "My hull can't take much more!  Help me out!"

949, "I don't think I'm gonna make it..."

950, "Sensors are picking up Vasudan ships 1.4 kilometers from our position.  Alpha wing, provide cover."

951, "We're already on it."

952, "We better get relieved soon.  I can't take much more."

953, "I really wasn't expecting this much action."

954, "My sensors are out, Alpha 1.  Aiming manually."

955, "Goddamnit!  I'm losing navigation!  I need you to cover me, Alpha 1!"

956, "Alpha - the area appears to be secure.  You may return to base. [Press $Alt-J$]"

957, "Another wing of hostiles just arrived!"

958, "We're taking hits.  Please provide cover."

959, "Get over here and cover us, Alpha!"

960, "Oh my God.  The Orff is down!  Return to the Galatea now, Alpha."

961, "Don't forget to use your heat seekers.  They have a range of 1500 meters."

962, "We've lost Alpha 2!"

963, "Aries is led by a Seth class fighter.  Watch out for him."

964, "Pisces wing is Horus Interceptors.  Use your MX-50s on them."

965, "Looks like this sector is clear.  Return to base."

966, "If you are going to stay on watch, you ought to rearm. [Press $Shift-R$]"

967, "Command said you needed some help."

968, "Moving into position now."

969, "Moving in to dock."

970, "Delta jumping out."

971, "Entering subspace now."

972, "Jumping out, sir."

973, "We've docked.  Give us some time to brace the attachment."

974, "The engine subsystems are back up and running."

975, "All systems go, sir."

976, "Operation ETC ninety seconds."

977, "Return to base."

978, "All objectives accomplished.  Return to base."

979, "Area is secured.  Return to base."

980, "The area is secure.  Report back to base."

981, "You've done all you can.  Return to the Galatea."

982, "Primary objective complete.  Secondary objective complete.  Return to base."

983, "What in the hell?!  Have you lost your mind?  Return to the Galatea now, Alpha!"

984, "Vasudan fighter wing Aries is destroyed."

985, "Enemy fighter wing down."

986, "Enemy wing destroyed."

987, "A fourteen year war between the Terrans and Vasudans leads into something far more sinister.  This is the story of the Great War."

988, "The main FreeSpace 2 campaign is unavailable.  Please deactivate the FreeSpace Port mod to play it."

989, "Special Operations Command has selected you for a dangerous covert assignment. Will you accept?"

990, "Special Operations Command requests your participation in a high-risk rescue mission. Will you volunteer?"

991, "Bringing The Hammer Down"

992, "Part 1 of the Templar Campaign.  An assault on a Hammer of Light Destroyer."

993, "$b * $b GTD $b Nereid
$b * $b Vasuda $b System
$b * $b 03/17/45

$b Operation $b Templar

Congratulations, pilot.  Because of your excellent service record, you have been chosen to participate in Operation Templar.  This is a joint Terran-Vasudan endeavor intended to eradicate the last remnants of the Vasudan fanatics who call themselves the Hammer of Light."

994, "$b New $b Technologies

Since losing contact with Earth, availability of the Avenger and Prometheus cannons has been extremely limited.  A Terran-Vasudan research group has developed a retrofit of the Prometheus using synthetic gases, sacrificing damage output.

The Prometheus R is being issued to all Alliance pilots as standard-issue weaponry."

995, "$b New $b Technologies

You are also issued the Akheton Subsystem Disruptor Gun.  It is highly effective against shielding and subsystems.

The Akheton is designed to function with Vasudan power grids.  You may need to allocate more energy to your weapons systems to fight effectively."

996, "$b New $b Technologies

Finally, the Serkr anti-capital ship torpedo has been put into mass production.  Developed by the GTI during the Hades Rebellion, the highly modular design is the most powerful warhead in our arsenal.

Older weapons reserves are limited, so choose your loadouts carefully."

997, "At 2130 hours, $h Hammer $h of $h Light operatives infiltrated Vasudan ranks in an attempt to hijack the $f GVD $f Anhur, a Typhon-class destroyer in the Vasuda system.  Security forces are now battling the rebels for control of the ship.  Your mission is to provide cover for the marine transports that will dock with the $f Anhur and insert reinforcements."

998, "Supreme Admiral Khu and other high-ranking officers of the Admiralty were on board the $f Anhur for a demonstration of the Scarab stealth technology prototypes.  Should the rebels attempt to seize the prototypes or take the Admiralty hostage, we will need to act decisively."

999, "This is a terrible loss.  Your incompetence has resulted in the Hammer of Light escaping with the Anhur, high-level Vasudan hostages, and the stealth technology prototypes.  We are sending in another team to track them down.  You are dismissed."

1000, "Disable the Anhur before it can depart.  Delta wing's bombers can help."

1001, "Great work, pilot!  The remnants of the Hammer of Light forces are on the run.  We are currently pursuing them into the Alpha Centauri system."

1002, "You prevented the Hammer of Light from escaping with the captured destroyer.  They will be that much weaker when we meet them again.  But that provides little comfort to those lost on the Anhur.  We must somehow eliminate this scourge once and for all!"

1003, "You did not have orders to return to base.  By deserting your unit, you have jeopardized this mission.  Consider yourself grounded until you can be court-martialed, pilot."

1004, "Don't leave until you are ordered to."

1005, "Hostages"

1006, "Stealth Prototypes"

