1482, "Field of Destruction"

1483, "Escort Iota through an asteroid field to a secret GTI safe spot."

1484, "Iota wing is en route to a GTI safe zone, located within an asteroid field.  We have positioned Watchdog sentries near the zone to neutralize incoming projectiles."

1485, "Iota's cargo is classified at the highest level, as are the coordinates of the safe zone.  Your orders are to rendezvous with Iota and follow them to their destination."

1486, "Well done.  Iota wing arrived at the safe zone and sustained minimal casualties.  You accomplished a mission of the utmost importance to GTI security."

1487, "Whose side are you on, pilot?  Iota was pulverized out there.  I am not authorized to discuss the consequences of this debacle, but Hammer of Light just named a cruiser after you."

1488, "Watch for bombers and let your wingmen handle the asteroids."

1489, "We suffered heavy losses, but the survivors of Iota wing owe you their lives."

1490, "Destroy Krishna"

1491, "Destroy Indra"

1492, "Escort Iota through the asteroid field."

1493, "We've lost Iota 1!"

1494, "Iota 2 has been destroyed!"

1495, "Iota 3 is gone!"

1496, "Gunnery's off line!  We got nothing here!"

1497, "Exodus"

1498, "GTI fighters have disabled the Krios!  Vital systems going critical!  Return to base pronto!"

1499, "Well done.  The evacuation could have been a massacre, but you got those pods to the jump node safely."

1500, "All escape pods were destroyed.  We are deeply saddened by the loss of this brave crew."

1501, "Order your wingmen to protect the pods, and engage the fighters as soon as possible."

1502, "A handful of escape pods survived the engagement.  We regret that more could not be recovered."

1503, "Destroy Bragi"

1504, "Destroy Hrid"

1505, "Destroy Buri"

1506, "Destroy Geri"

1507, "Destroy Scald"

1508, "Protect the Destroyer"

1509, "All remaining escape pods have safely reached the jump node.  Return to base."

1510, "All escape pods have been destroyed.  Return to base."

1511, "Krios suffered catastrophic hull failure.  I got forty-three crew in escape pods, and we're flying to the jump node."

1512, "The Krios is going down.  Defend the escape pods!"

1513, "Alpha!  Beta!  We need cover!  Now!  They'll butcher us out here!"

1514, "Engage GTI cruiser Vidar.  Keep those gunners occupied till the pods reach the jump node."

1515, "The Return to Ross 128"

1516, "The Fate of the Krios

To obliterate data gathered about its activities in the Ross 128 system, Galactic Terran Intelligence destroyed the Krios.  Effectively immediately, all surviving personnel are to be reassigned to the GTD Soyakaze."

1517, "The GTI

The conspiracy is not confined to a rogue element within the GTI, but involves officers in the highest echelon of the intelligence directorate.  Although their objectives remain unclear, Command believes the conspirators intend to overthrow the GTA government and dissolve the Terran-Vasudan Treaty.

Galatic Terran Intelligence-its ships, installations, and personnel-are now hostile targets.  Because of the  technology and sensitive information within its grasp, the GTI poses a significant threat to the stability and security of the GTA, the PVN, and all allied worlds.  Our actions must be swift and decisive.

The Soyakaze's primary objective is to locate and destroy the GTI's base of operations."

1518, "Ross 128

The Soyakaze has set course for the Ross 128 system.  Information recovered from the Krios indicates GTI operations are concentrated around the site of the initial Shivan attack.  Our first task will be to investigate this activity."

1519, "Admiral Scott

I will now take this opportunity to honor the late Admiral Scott, commander of the GTD Krios, who died in the line of duty.

Admiral Scott devoted many years of service to the GTI and dedicated himself to its mission: to provide the GTA and its allies with accurate and comprehensive information regarding the tactics, technologies, activities, and strategic objectives of its enemies.

His superiors, to whom he had given his trust and loyalty, betrayed Admiral Scott when they abandoned that mission to pursue their corrupt ambitions and designs.  GTI is now the enemy.

Let us never forget the integrity and sacrifice of this fine officer."

1520, "New Technology: EM Pulse Missile

Without the technology and expertise of GTI's research and development branch, we will lack our enemy's cutting-edge weapon systems and ship prototypes.  However, we do have a new addition to the arsenal: the EM Pulse missile.

Upon impact, the EM Pulse disables the electronics systems of the target ship.  The weapon has numerous tactical applications.  For example, a direct hit with an EM Pulse missile will prevent bombers from launching aspect-seeking warheads for several seconds.  Once the EMP field has worn off, they must also reacquire their target's signature lock."

1521, "We have set course for Ross 128, the site of the first Shivan contact.  GTI operatives have been active in this system, and we must investigate.  Your mission will be to inspect the wreckage from the original Shivan assault."

1522, "Ross 128 is currently under Shivan control.  There are no other Terran forces in this system.  You will need to complete your mission quickly.  Scan the wreckage and return to base."

1523, "Your wing annihilated all GTI vessels.  Fine work.  We suspect the GTI already salvaged the wreckage at Ross 128.  Their objectives in this sector remain unknown."

1524, "We made no strategic gains at Ross 128, but your assault decimated the Shivan garrison.  Nice work."

1525, "Use the Shivans to your advantage against the GTI."

1526, "Elements of the Shivan force escaped.  I should not have to remind you that destroying all hostiles is a high priority.  Winning the battle means nothing if we lose the war."

1527, "Destroy Vishnu"

1528, "Destroy the GTI craft."

1529, "Destroy all remaining Shivans"

1530, "Inspect Remaining Wreckage"

1531, "Sensors indicate Terran configurations.  Request immediate verification.  We're the only Terran presence confirmed in this area."

1532, "Terran vessels are GTI ships.  Engage and destroy all hostiles - GTI and Shivan."

1533, "Hostiles have been neutralized, but sensors are unable to locate wreckage for scanning.  Abort mission and return to base."

1534, "The Wait"

1535, "Reconnaissance reports heavy Shivan traffic through the Beta Aquilae jump node.  Our mission: shut them down."

1536, "Your wing will patrol this area and engage any hostiles.  Seek and destroy."

1537, "You had orders not to destroy the cargo, pilot.  Either you're a slow learner or you're shooting for demotion.  Intelligence needed that cargo for analysis."

1538, "Disable the freighters first, then destroy them after eliminating the other hostiles."

1539, "The Shivans escaped with their cargo.  Apparently their freighters were too fast and maneuverable for you, pilot.  Command is unimpressed with your lack of results."

1540, "Our freighters retrieved the Shivan cargo.  Well done.  Intelligence has begun its analysis, and we hope to learn much about Shivan strategy in this sector."

1541, "We failed to recover all the cargo, but we have sufficient evidence to uncover the Shivan's objective in this sector."

1542, "Unknown"

1543, "Destroy Asura"

1544, "Patrol area for Shivan activity"

1545, "Retrieve the Shivan cargo"

1546, "Destroy all Shivan forces"

1547, "Shivans jumping in.  We got a great big convoy"

1548, "Are we just gonna sit here and wait?"

1549, "Command says Shivans have been swarming all over this node."

1550, "Engage and destroy Shivan freighters.  Do not, repeat, do not destroy the cargo.  We will commence retrieval once the area is secured."

1551, "Deploying freighters Priam, Hector, and Paris to retrieve the cargo."

1552, "The freighters can take it from here.  Return to base."

1553, "Alpha, stop wasting time and return to base"

1554, "Back off!  That cruiser's gonna blow!"

1555, "Secrets Revealed"

1556, "GTI Headquarters

We have located the GTI's base of operations- the Jotunheim installation in the Beta Aquilae system.

The full extent of their activities in Beta Aquilae remain unknown.  However, we believe the GTI has been studying Shivan culture and technology at Jotunheim since the massacre at Ross 128."

1557, "GTI Plans

Reconnaissance also has evidence of a large-scale prototype construction involving Shivan technology, but no data regarding the configuration and capability of this vessel could be gathered."

1558, "GTI Technology

GTI forces have access to Shivan armaments as well as the systems created by its research and development branch, so be advised your foe will possess superior technology.  You will have to fly smarter and fight harder to win this battle.

Command suspects the GTI may also have Shivan captives at Jotunheim for the purposes of biological research and the development of viral weapons."

1559, "Hades

Terran Command intercepted a GTI transmission and technical readout relating to a Jotunheim operation with the codename Project Hades.  Cryptographers are in the process of deciphering the transmission, and engineers are analyzing the technical readout.  Although we have nothing conclusive, we must act now."

1560, "Our Mission

The rogue Galactic Terran Intelligence group must be crushed.  These traitors threaten the security of the GTA, the stability of the Terran-Vasudan Alliance, and our future victory over the Shivans.  Report for your mission briefing, pilot."

1561, "Reconnaissance has uncovered the location of GTI's primary base of operations, the Jotunheim.  Details concerning the strength of the garrison remain sketchy.  GTA will launch an immediate, all-out offensive and deploy reinforcements as soon as possible."

1562, "Failure is not an option.  The GTI conducts weapons research on the Jotunheim, so be prepared to engage exotic prototypes with unknown capabilities."

1563, "Your cowardice jeopardized our best opportunity to eliminate the GTI threat.  Once operational, the Shivan-Terran hybrid will be invincible.  Dismissed, pilot."

1564, "Protect your bombers and keep your wingmen focused."

1565, "Excellent work!  Our initiative caught the GTI off guard.  Preliminary scans indicate the GTI possessed Shivan defensive technologies.  If that juggernaut had gone on line, GTI would be writing the history books."

1566, "For conspicuous gallantry at the risk of your own life, you have distinguished yourself above and beyond the call of duty in the highest traditions of military service.  You are hereby awarded the Galactic Service Medal, the most prestigious honor bestowed by the Galactic Terran Alliance."

1567, "That sucked, didn't it?  Well, if you share our feelings that Silent Threat had potential that it never managed to live up to, then you might like to try Silent Threat: Reborn.  ST:R is the Port team's reimagined and reinterpreted version of Silent Threat, with improved missions, a deeper plot, more immersion, and plenty of ties to FreeSpace 2!  Visit the Port website hosted at Hard Light Productions for more information."

