2573, "All wings ready.  Commencing attack."

2574, "We have engaged the enemy forces.  Destroy the Eva ASAP."

2575, "We need your assistance.  Stand by for new orders."

2576, "Doomsday"

2577, "The Galatea is under fire from Shivan forces and looks sure to be lost.  Long range sensors indicate at least four wings of bombers and interceptors.  The Lucifer is also somewhere in the area.  The Galatea must be protected until we can evacuate the personnel."

2578, "Good job destroying the Eva."

2579, "The Galatea has been destroyed.  Many lives, many friends are gone.  Everyone in the Terran Alliance feel this loss deeply.

Yet, greater is the tragedy of the Vasudans.  There is nothing between the Shivan fleet and Vasuda Prime.  Soon their homeworld will be gone.

Our fighters fought bravely to preserve the Galatea, but there was nothing to be done.  The Lucifer was too powerful."

2580, "The Galatea has been destroyed.  Not by the hand of a cruiser or a destroyer.  But by a bomber.  This is truly a sad day for the Alliance.  If a squadron of bombers can destroy one of our flagships, how can we defeat the Lucifer?"

2581, "Protect the Galatea from the bombers at all costs.  Attack the Nephilims before worrying about the Manticores.  Shooting down the Nephilim's bombs will preserve the Galatea even longer.  If you managed to save some Synaptic bombs from the Eva attack, use them now."

2582, "You fled the most important battle of your career.  The Galatea has been lost and the people of Vasuda Prime are doomed.

Such cowardice is unconscionable.  You are permanently grounded."

2583, "At least make an attempt to save the Galatea!"

2584, "Many lives were saved by the Hermes escape pods.  For that we are thankful.  But we mourn the loss of Admiral Wolf.  He was a great commander and he died with the ship he loved.

All surviving pilots are reassigned to the GTD Bastion.  Though we all lost friends on the Galatea, there is no time to mourn the dead.  The fate of the Alliance is grim."

2585, "For surviving the death of your capital ship, and saving the lives of many others due to this, the GTA has awarded you the Galatea Survivor."

2586, "Countless lives were lost in the destruction of the Galatea.  The Shivans even destroyed many of the escape pods.

All surviving pilots are reassigned to the GTD Bastion.  Though we all lost friends on the Galatea, there is no time to mourn the dead.  We hope for the chance to avenge their deaths."

2587, "While the Galatea's demise is imminent, the escape pods themselves can be saved.  Prevent them from dying.  Focus all your firepower on Krishna."

2588, "Evacuate"

2589, "Protect The GTD Galatea"

2590, "Protect the Escaping Escape Pods"

2591, "We beginning the evacuation sequence.  Keep them away from the escape pods!"

2592, "Evacuate the area immediately.  We are transmitting the coordinates for the Bastion."

2593, "We are getting pounded hard!"

2594, "We can't take many more hits."

2595, "We've lost an escape pod!  Protect them!"

2596, "Clear the area, we're not going to make it!"

2597, "Good God!  We've lost the Galatea."

2598, "The Lucifer just arrived!"

2599, "Act 3, Mission 1"

2600, "$b * $b GTD $b Bastion
$b * $b Alpha $b Centauri $b System
$b * $b 3/1/35

$b New $b Assignments

This is Admiral Shima.  I'll be delivering your command briefs while you're onboard the GTD Bastion.  I extend a welcome to all pilots formerly stationed on the Galatea.  I wish your reassignments could have come under better circumstances.

The loss of the Galatea is a great blow to all of us.  We've lost many friends and loved ones.  We've also lost many great pilots.  We will need to double our efforts if we plan on stopping the Shivan fleet."

2601, "$b Destruction $b of $b Vasuda $b Prime

This brings me to the reason for this briefing.  As some of you may have already heard, shortly after the destruction of the Galatea at nineteen-hundred last night, we received word that the Shivan Lucifer made the jump to Vasuda Prime.  The Lucifer fleet bombarded Vasuda Prime from orbit for thirteen hours straight."

2602, "$b Aftermath $b of $b Vasuda $b Attack

Most escaping transport ships were destroyed.  All major Vasudan cities were leveled, and most of the landmass was rendered uninhabitable.  All of our attacks launched from the nearby installations were defeated.

We have lost contact with all Terran ships in the area, but it appears that the Shivan fleet has now moved on.  It's estimated that four billion innocent Vasudans lost their lives in the attack.

Terran Command is preparing to help evacuate all survivors to other habitable worlds in the area."

2603, "$b Our $b Orders

What we need to concentrate on now is keeping the Lucifer fleet from making further moves towards Earth.  We've been put on standby status and ordered to assist in all evacuation operations in Vasuda Prime and the surrounding systems.

We've lost Deneb.  Antares is virtually undefended.  Vasuda is a contested system."

2604, "$b New $b Technology: $b Banshee $b Laser

The Banshee laser is now ready for deployment.  We just received a partial shipment of them.  The Banshee is specifically designed to take down Shivan shields."

2605, "$b New $b Technology: $b Hornet $b Swarm $b Missile

We have also received a full supply of Hornet Swarm missiles.  These are the best anti-fighter missiles in our arsenal, and we expect they will receive heavy use on the Bastion.  Full details are available in the Tech Room."

2606, "Pilot Attend:  As you know, Vasuda Prime has been devastated.  Our focus must now shift to the evacuation of the survivors.  You are to take your wing to the subspace node cluster in the Alpha Centauri system."

2607, "Vasudan warships will travel to and from both the Sirius and Vasuda jump points."

2608, "You did an outstanding job in protecting the Vasudan transports.  Through your actions we were able to save countless lives.  You should feel proud of this accomplishment."

2609, "Far too many ships were lost in this evacuation operation.  This is a great blow to the Vasudan morale and will put an enormous strain on the Terran-Vasudan relations.  It is unfortunate that you were unable to do more to help those refugees."

2610, "However, we were not able to secure the area because you left your post before you were relieved.  This is not the kind of performance we have come to expect from you.  Perhaps our trust in your abilities is misplaced."

2611, "Remain in the area until Zeta arrives to relieve you.  If worse comes to worst, Delta wing is available for reinforcements."

2612, "Remain in the area until Zeta wing has arrived to relieve you.  If you are having difficulty staying alive that long, make sure you manage your shields well.  If worse comes to worst, you may call in Delta wing to assist you."

2613, "We did lose a few refugee ships during this evacuation operation.  We have contacted the PVE and expressed our regrets."

2614, "We are pleased you were able to use Delta wing to accomplish all of your objectives.  However, you should try to keep your use of reinforcements at a minimum.  If every wing commander leader requested reinforcements at every opportunity, we would run out of fighters."

2615, "Escort Mu"

2616, "Escort Theta"

2617, "Escort Kappa"

2618, "Protect Mecross"

2619, "Destroy Hostiles"

2620, "Destroy Cruisers"

2621, "Alpha, listen up.  The Shivans are trying to stop the vessels leaving Vasuda Prime."

2622, "The Vasudans are sending armed transports to deal with the Shivan threat.  We are also sending a wing of freighters to resupply them."

2623, "It is critical that these freighters make it to their destination.  You must ensure they make it safely to their jump points.  Carry on Alpha 1."

2624, "Listen up Alpha 1.  The Vasudans are sending in the Mecross to help secure the area."

2625, "You will stay with the Mecross until additional fighters can be sent to relieve your post.  Protect the Mecross at all costs."

2626, "The Mecross has been destroyed!"

2627, "Second Shivan cruiser has been eliminated."

2628, "The PVD Hope is leaving the Antares system after an intense battle.  It has sustained moderate damage and will be jumping to the Beta Aquilae system."

2629, "We are sending two wings to help cover the Hope while it is being repaired.  The Vasudans are sending their own fighters to stand guard over the Hope, but it will be some time before they arrive."

2630, "The Hope should be in the system when you arrive.  We do not believe the Shivans have enough forces in the system to mount a serious attack, but their strategies are difficult to predict.  Good luck."

2631, "Well done, Pilot.  This mission was quite a bit more intense than we had expected, thanks to the Shivans.  Fortunately you were able to hang on until the Vasudan reinforcements arrived.  Very impressive."

2632, "Guard PVD Hope"

2633, "...serious damage.  Please assist."

2634, "You should try to stay near the escape pods and destroy any Shivan fighters that attack them.  Sacrificing one or two pods so the rest can make it is a wise choice which you may have to make."

2635, "You can't save the installation, but you can save the Communications Terminal.  Try your hardest to kill the bombers before they can launch missiles at it.  Don't be afraid to switch targets even if you haven't finished off one of the bombers.  Just don't let them get a bead on the comm station."

2636, "Destroy Deva"

2637, "Destroy Karna"

2638, "Escape 2 didn't make it."

2639, "We lost escape 4!"

2640, "In a last ditch effort to stave off the Shivan attack, Terran Command pursues all the leads that it has.  One such lead takes the player and his squadron deep into conquered Vasudan territory in order to recover an ancient artifact.  Half the challenge, however, is getting there..."

2641, "$b * $b GTD $b Bastion
$b * $b Ribos $b System
$b * $b 3/2/35

$b State $b of $b the $b Alliance

We have now lost vital ground to the Shivans in the Antares system and Sirius.  The number of systems between the Shivans and Earth are dwindling fast.  Fortunately, we were able to save the Beta Aquilae communications terminal.  Aside from that single post, we have lost communications with every outer colony."

2642, "$b Transmission $b from $b Altair

The following transmission was picked up by the Terran listening outpost in the Beta Aquilae system.

''...We are a group of Vasudan refugees seeking the assistance of any Terran ships.  We were onboard a Vasudan science outpost when it was destroyed by the Shivans.  We managed to land on this uncharted planet when our escape pod lost power.  It's uninhabited, but we uncovered the remains of an ancient civilization.  They were neither Terran nor Vasudan nor Shivan."

2643, "$b Transmission $b Continued

''Our scanning equipment was able to locate a storage device of some sort.  It was heavily protected, which suggests it stores something quite valuable, possibly information or technology.  We are attempting to decipher the language of the device, but are fearful of Shivan attacks."

2644, "$b Transmission $b Continued

''I say this because it is immediately apparent that this planet was also destroyed by Shivan weapons.  This is difficult to believe, considering the age of the remains, but the evidence is conclusive.  What we ask is for rescue and an escort away from this planet.  Our scientists are not normally a superstitious group, but having one's homeworld destroyed tends to shake your beliefs.  Please send an armed rescue as soon as possible to these coordinates.''"

2645, "$b Our $b Orders

Your next series of missions will require both massive firepower and intelligence.  For this reason, I am assigning Alpha 1 to lead these missions.  We will be attempting to rescue the Vasudan refugees from Altair."

2646, "$b New $b Technology: $b Jump $b Drives

This mission will be facilitated by the new subspace drive we have received.  For years the GTA has tried to give a fighter the ability to do intersystem jumps.  After monitoring the Beta Aquilae engagements, the GTA science colony at Sol has finally been able to solve the puzzle.  All GTA fighters are currently being equipped with intersystem subspace drives."

2647, "$b New $b Technology: $b Project $b Ursa

Research and Development have nearly completed project Ursa, which should be our best bet at defeating the Shivan Lucifer destroyer.  For those of you that haven't been keeping up, Project Ursa is an attempt to make a new type of heavy bomber capable of carrying the Harbinger bomb.

We expect that a wing of Ursas will be available to you on your return trip from Altair."

2648, "$b New $b Technology: $b Harbinger $b Bomb

The Harbinger will assist us greatly in any attacks against capital ships.  Until recently, Harbingers were reserved for planetary attacks only.  With this project nearing completion, we may be able to finally defeat the Lucifer."

2649, "$b New $b Technology: $b Disruptor $b Missile

You may or may not want to use the new Disruptor Missile to assist you in the next few missions.  It is the only missile in our arsenal which allows us to completely shut down a cruiser for a short amount of time.  It's definitely worth a look.  Details are in the Tech Room."

2650, "After you have completed these tasks, stand by for further orders.  Good luck, Alpha 1."

2651, "You were ordered to stay in the area until you received further orders.  Yet you jumped out and the mission is a failure.  You are hereby grounded.  Dismissed."

2652, "Stay in the area and await further orders.  If you can't beat the Zenith, try to first eliminate all Dragons in the area, then go straight for the Zenith's comms.  Once the comms are out, target the weapons system and then allow your bombers to finish him off."

2653, "Destroy Zenith"

2654, "Disarm Zenith"

2655, "Destroy Benedict"

2656, "Shivans are requesting reinforcements.  We need to destroy the Zenith's comms ASAP."

2657, "Target has been disarmed sir.  Should we attack or warp out?"

2658, "Looks like the sector is clear.  Standby for new orders."

2659, "In a last ditch effort to stave off the Shivan attack, Terran Command pursues all the leads that it has.  One such lead takes the player and his squadron deep into conquered Vasudan territory in order to recover an ancient artifact.  And while the preliminaries are complete, the chances of this operation going off without a hitch are all but... nil."

2660, "As you already know, we are sending scientists to the Altair system to investigate records found on Altair IV.  Command hopes they will aid us in our war with the Shivans.

The Rosetta is currently carrying the scientists.  It will rendezvous with two transports, Omega 1 and Omega 2.  All three ships should be arriving within a few minutes.

Omega wing will dock with the Rosetta as soon as they arrive.  Oversee this personnel transfer, then escort Omega 1 and Omega 2 to the jump node."

2661, "Forget Rosetta.  Getting those two transports out alive is far more important.  You have to take out those heavy attack Basilisks as fast as possible, before they launch their streams of swarm missiles."

2662, "Oversee Omega 1 docking"

2663, "Oversee Omega 2 docking"

2664, "Escort Omega 1 to Jump Node"

2665, "Escort Omega 2 to Jump Node"

2666, "The player and his squadron simply have to ensure that the scientists and records make it back home.  It's too bad that the Hammer of Light believes that the Terrans have overstayed their welcome."

2667, "We have successfully extracted the records from Altair IV.  They have been partially deciphered and are being moved back to Terran Space.  Omega transports will once again be handling the movement of the scientists and the records."

2668, "We have successfully extracted the records from Altair IV.  They have been partially deciphered and are being moved back to Terran Space.  Omega will once again be handling the movement of the scientists and the records."

2669, "If worse comes to worst, let Omega 2 die, and go straight for the Leo bombers.  Once you've destroyed the first wave of Leos, you can simply order everyone to engage fighters, and you should have little trouble escorting Omega 1 to the jump node."

2670, "If you are having trouble keeping both transports alive, keep this in mind:  The Leo squadron of bombers has only 4 bombers, and no reinforcements.  Destroy them as quickly as possible, and you are free to worry about Omega 2.  If you can't destroy the Typhon, at least try to disable it with disruptor missiles while Omega 2 flies by."

2671, "Anvil taking a pounding.  Just a few more bombs."

2672, "Clash of the Titans"

2673, "$b * $b GTD $b Bastion
$b * $b Sirius $b System
$b * $b 3/29/35

$b The $b Lucifer

The Shivans have finally determined the location of the Sol system.  The Lucifer has moved into position here in Sirius for the subspace jump to Delta Serpentis.

From Delta Serpentis, she will certainly  make the jump to Sol to destroy our homeworld."

2674, "$b New $b Information

From the records you retrieved in Altair, we have discovered the means to destroy the Lucifer.  As you know, our shield systems do not work in subspace.  The same holds true for the Lucifer.  More importantly, the records contain the information to enable us to track a capital ship into and inside subspace.

If we can track the Lucifer into subspace, we believe a small strike force may be sufficient to destroy it."

2675, "$b Our $b Orders

We have been assigned the task of destroying the Lucifer before she reaches Sol.  The Bastion is currently en route to intercept the Lucifer at the Sirius-Delta Serpentis subspace node.

The Bastion will attempt to provide close cover, while Ursa bombers deliver a payload of Harbingers.  We believe that without the shielding system it's relied on so heavily, the Lucifer will be vulnerable.

Keep in mind that this is a time critical operation.  If we do not enter subspace soon after the Lucifer, we cannot launch our attack."

2676, "$b Destroying $b the $b Lucifer

From your earlier scans of the Lucifer in the Deneb system, we have determined that it is powered by five primary reactors.  These reactors are spread out across the Lucifer.

If all five reactors are destroyed in a short period of time, the Lucifer won't have a chance of surviving."

2677, "We don't have much time.  Report for mission briefings immediately."

2678, "We have few chances to stop the $h Lucifer.  It is heading to the Sol system but we have an opportunity to head them off at Sirius."

2679, "If you encounter the Lucifer in Sirius, hold it off until the rest of the fleet can catch up with you."

2680, "The Bastion was severely damaged in this battle.  More of the burden of destroying the Lucifer will shift to the bombers.  The Bastion will be of limited assistance.

We are now proceeding to the Delta Serpentis system."

2681, "Try to destroy all bombers before they reach the Bastion."

2682, "The GTD Bastion is in prime condition to assault the Lucifer.  We are proceeding to Delta Serpentis now."

2683, "For your outstanding defense of the GTD Bastion, you are awarded the Military Defense Medal."

2684, "The Bastion has been destroyed.  There is little hope of stopping the Lucifer at this point.  This is the saddest of days for the Alliance.  The Lucifer is expected to reach Earth in 40 hours."

2685, "Always kill the bombers first.  Try shooting down their bombs.  You cannot let the Bastion die at this stage of the war."

2686, "The Bastion made the jump to Delta Serpentis and you didn't you follow her?  She was destroyed shortly after her arrival.  We have no way of stopping the Lucifer.  This is certainly the end of the Alliance.  The Lucifer is expected to reach Earth in 40 hours."

2687, "After the Bastion departs, make sure you jump out inside the jump node."

2688, "Warp Out at Node"

2689, "Escort GTD Bastion to the Lucifer"

2690, "Keep the GTD Bastion's hull above 35%"

2691, "Destroy the SD Tantalus"

2692, "No sign of the Lucifer.  We'll have to proceed to Delta Serpentis."

2693, "Hull integrity is dropping.  We need support."

2694, "I don't know how much more damage we can take."

2695, "The Bastion has been destroyed.  Return to the Delta Serpentis."

2696, "Entering subspace now.  We will rendezvous with you there."

2697, "This looks like an ambush!"

2698, "Protect the Bastion!"

2699, "Go to the subspace node and depart, Alpha."

2700, "The Great Hunt"

2701, "In a few minutes we will be entering the Delta Serpentis sector.  We will then begin the most important engagement in our history.  We will fight for the very survival of Earth."

2702, "Our plan is to rapidly close the distance with the Lucifer so that the Bastion will be able to enter subspace just behind her.  Once in subspace, we will attack and destroy the Lucifer."

2703, "Your task will be to provide cover for the Bastion so that it can quickly converge on the Lucifer.

That destroyer must be stopped at all costs.  Failure is absolutely not an option here, pilots.  Good luck."

2704, "Why you chose to leave the battle area is a complete mystery.  If any historians survive the destruction of Earth, they will surely wonder what went through your mind.

In a battle for the fate of Earth, you fled like a coward."

2705, "You must be within range of the jump point before you make your jump.  Terran Command will inform you when you are within range."

2706, "Escort Delta to Node"

2707, "Reach the Subspace Node"

2708, "Escort the Bastion to the Jump Node"

2709, "There's the Lucifer!  It's powering up to leave the system."

2710, "Alpha 1!  You must clear out these enemy fighters as quickly as possible!  We've got to catch up with the Lucifer!"

2711, "It's no use!  The Bastion will never catch up with the Lucifer.  You'll have to go after it yourself, Alpha 1."

2712, "We're launching four Ursas armed with Harbinger bombs.  We can only pray they'll be enough."

2713, "We are readying four Thoths to help provide cover.  As soon as they're ready we'll deploy them."

2714, "Alpha 1.  The Thoths are ready and on the way."

2715, "You have roughly 10 minutes to reach the jump point.  Beyond that you will not have enough time to defeat the Lucifer."

2716, "God speed, Alpha!"

2717, "Alpha 1!  You've got about seven minutes left!  Hurry!"

2718, "You've only got about four minutes left!  Move it, pilot!"

2719, "Alpha 1,  If you don't jump in the next minute, everything is lost!  Please, make the jump."

2720, "Thank God.  Our hopes and prayers are with you, Alpha 1."

2721, "Epsilon here, don't wait for us, Alpha.  Keep going.  We'll try to catch up with you."

2722, "We're never going to make it in time!"

2723, "Keep quiet!  We have no other option, pilot!"

2724, "Keep moving!  Go!  Go!"

2725, "You're almost there, Alpha!"

2726, "That's it, Alpha 1.  We have no chance of getting the Lucifer now.  Earth is doomed."

2727, "All right fellas'.  Let's plow the field!"

2728, "You've made it Alpha 1!  Your jump drives are powering up now."

2729, "Good Luck"

2730, "Your objective is to destroy the Lucifer.  The Lucifer has five reactors located on its main hull.  In order to eliminate the Lucifer, these reactors must be destroyed."

2731, "This stage will never be seen, and if you are looking at it, ignore it.  Red Alert missions only have one stage."

2732, "Congratulations on finishing the game."

